# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# WSL/Windows "mark of the web" alternate-data-stream artifacts
*:Zone.Identifier

# Brian2 network state dumps (net.store()/restore()) -- these carry full
# monitor history, so they routinely run 150-175MB, over GitHub's 100MB
# per-file limit. Regenerable: baseline_2hz.bri via the notebooks' own
# calibration cells, seed_robustness/results/baselines/*.bri via
# `python seed_robustness/run_seed_check.py`.
*.bri

# seed_robustness pipeline: per-process scratch (each job's isolated cwd,
# holding a throwaway copy of that seed's baseline) and the compiled Cython
# extensions (machine/architecture-specific, not portable, not source).
# Keep results/{raw,traces,reference,plots,summary.csv} -- those are the
# actual outputs (small, worth versioning for the paper).
seed_robustness/results/work/
seed_robustness/results/cython_cache/
